# 0095-export-without-p12.patch -- a build no longer needs the .p12: with no signing identity on this install the chain signs the framework AD HOC, for export only. Applies after 0094.
# UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# Why: with a distribution certificate a built game cannot be played inside iBuilder anyway (iOS refuses to map code from the app's Documents); the player builds, then "Export as its own
# app" (IPA), and the installer (SideStore / AltStore / a provider) RE-SIGNS the whole IPA, frameworks included. So the .p12 is needed only to Play inside iBuilder.
# The chain (ibuilder-pipeline stage 4b, assemble::adhoc_fallback): when the signer finds no identity (rc 10 no embedded.mobileprovision, 12 no certificate, 13 no .p12) it signs the
# framework ad hoc (ibuilder_options.sign_adhoc: the shim's zsign ad hoc mode, the simulator's) and stamps it "signature=adhoc-export"; no boot starts from such a framework (after the
# build, boot-only, or at launch). rc 11, 14 and 20 (a .p12 that is there and cannot be used) still fail. With a .p12 nothing changes (the same signing call, the stamp's four lines).
# The app:
#   * the certificate row is information, not a prerequisite ("needed only to Play inside iBuilder"): no banner, the Settings tile says "Not imported" (no red);
#   * a build signed for export only (UiFacts.ExportOnlyGames: the stamp in Documents and the parked ones) is Export IPA only, never Play (no dlopen is tried), with the line "Built for
#     export: import your .p12 to play inside iBuilder, or export the IPA." under its buttons and in its sheet; the build screen says "Ready to export", the notification "Built for export";
#   * a .p12 imported later: the game's sheet offers "Sign again to play" (gameapp_sign_framework_again: the framework signed with the identity as stage 4b does, no rebuild; the stamp then
#     loses its signature= line and the game plays). Not offered with a distribution certificate (it could not play here anyway).
#   * the export (GameAppExport.cs) needed no change: it drops the framework's _CodeSignature and Info.plist, writes its own Info.plist, and the Mach-O keeps its ad hoc signature, which an
#     installer replaces like any other; nothing in the export reads the identity.
#
# VERIFIED (M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: 0010-0096 apply in order, no fuzz, no offset. Compile (-t:Compile, ios-arm64): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same codes as 0094. Host harness
#   (target/agent-work/feat-p12-bc/h96): 56 of 56 checks (0095 and 0096); harness94 still 358 of 358 on the patched tree; 8 of 8 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: a real build with no .p12, an exported IPA installed by SideStore / a provider, a real "Sign again" with zsign.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Built for export: import your .p12 to play inside iBuilder, or export the IPA.", "Sign again to play", "needed only to Play inside iBuilder", "Ready to export",
#   "Built for export: export the IPA", "Not imported"; log lines "sign again: ", "the built framework is signed for export only".
